# Design system / north star rule

The application has one shared product architecture and multiple interchangeable visual moods.

Current default: Core — Editorial + Analytical + Entertainment (`core`).

Alternative moods:

- Editorial Observatory (`editorial-observatory`)
- Cinematic Archive (`cinematic-archive`)
- Modern Cultural Index (`modern-cultural-index`)
- Slightly Game-Native (`game-native`)

These are themes, not separate applications.

## Rules

1. Never hard-code theme-specific colors, typography, radii, shadows, spacing, or motion inside feature components.
2. Feature components consume semantic design tokens (CSS variables emitted from the theme contract).
3. Theme files provide token values. They live in `src/design-system/themes/`.
4. Every theme implements the same typed `Theme` contract in `src/design-system/theme-types.ts`.
5. Switching the active theme must require changing theme state or configuration, not editing feature components.
6. Do not duplicate pages or components for individual moods.
7. Preserve the same information architecture across moods.
8. Every new component must work under all themes.
9. Light/dark mode is independent of mood. Do not create a separate theme per combination.
10. Never use positive/negative semantic colors as brand colors. Accent means interaction. Green, amber, and red mean evaluation state, and never alone.
11. Interactive controls require `cursor: pointer` plus hover, focus-visible, active, disabled, and loading states where applicable.
12. Motion must be restrained and functional. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
13. If a new visual property is needed, first determine whether it belongs in the token system.
14. Do not introduce a one-off visual value merely because it is convenient.
15. Accessibility is required across every theme.
16. A theme experiment must never change product semantics or evaluation logic.
17. The visual system must never cause the work's artwork to become less important than site chrome.
18. Do not branch JSX on `theme === ...` unless the visual structure genuinely cannot be expressed with tokens. Prefer token changes.
19. Do not make theme switching a prominent public navigation item. Color mode may be quiet. Mood switching stays in the appearance control.
20. The default mood is `core`, overridable with `NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_MOOD`.
